      <div class="settings-section-body" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px;">
        
        <!-- Release Version 3.5.0 -->
        <div style="position: relative; padding-left: 20px; border-left: 2px solid var(--accent-primary);">
          <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px;">
            <h6 style="font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; color: #fff; margin: 0;">v3.5.0 <span class="lp-badge lp-badge-success" style="font-size: 9px; padding: 2px 6px;">Latest Release</span></h6>
            <span style="font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-muted);">August 31, 2026</span>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 8px;">
            Multi-Node Mesh &amp; Fleet Orchestration, Visual Docker Compose Studio, CrowdSec Community Defense, ZFS/Btrfs Instant Snapshots, Real-Time Multi-Channel Incident Alerting &amp; Auto-Remediation, and Advanced Database GUI Studio.
          </p>
          <ul style="font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-secondary); padding-left: 16px; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px;">
            <li><strong>Docker Compose Visual Studio &amp; Auto HTTPS:</strong> Visual 2-way form &amp; YAML synchronizer, stack logs tailing, environment variable matrix, and 1-Click Let's Encrypt / ZeroSSL auto-reverse proxy.</li>
            <li><strong>CrowdSec Community Defense &amp; Honeypot Traps:</strong> Integrated CrowdSec decisions sync, bad bot traps (<code>/.env</code>, <code>/.git</code>, <code>/wp-login.php</code>), RCE Shellshock filter, GeoIP shield, and 1-Click System Hardening.</li>
            <li><strong>Multi-Node Server Clustering &amp; Agent Mesh:</strong> Centralized multi-server fleet capacity aggregator, 1-Click cryptographic pairing tokens, one-line bootstrap installer, and parallel remote command dispatcher.</li>
            <li><strong>ZFS / Btrfs Instant Snapshots &amp; 1-Second Rollback:</strong> Point-in-time snapshot manager supporting LVM thin pools, ZFS datasets, and Btrfs subvolumes with instant rollback.</li>
            <li><strong>Multi-Channel Alerting &amp; Auto-Remediation:</strong> Broadcasts incidents to Telegram, Discord, Slack, WhatsApp, Email, and WebPush with automated incident remediation (Emergency Disk Cleanup, Dead Service Resurrect, OOM mitigation).</li>
            <li><strong>Advanced Database GUI Studio:</strong> Visual table browser with double-click inline cell editing, dynamic row insertion modal, safe row deletion, and interactive SQL Scratchpad with <code>EXPLAIN</code> query execution plan visualization.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Release Version 3.3.0 (Fase 5) -->
        <div style="position: relative; padding-left: 20px; border-left: 2px solid var(--accent-success);">
          <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px;">
            <h6 style="font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; color: #fff; margin: 0;">v3.3.0</h6>
            <span style="font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-muted);">August 29, 2026</span>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 8px;">
            Enterprise Observability &amp; K3s Kubernetes Cluster Inspector — Native OpenMetrics Prometheus Exporter (<code>/metrics</code>), K3s &amp; MicroK8s Pod &amp; Node Inspector, and Centralized Fleet Telemetry.
          </p>
          <ul style="font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-secondary); padding-left: 16px; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px;">
            <li><strong>Prometheus / OpenMetrics Exporter (Fase 5):</strong> Exposes real-time CPU cores, memory bytes, load averages, Docker containers, and active WAF rules formatted for Prometheus &amp; Grafana scraping at <code>/metrics</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Lightweight Kubernetes Inspector (Fase 5):</strong> Auto-detects local K3s and MicroK8s engines, enumerating cluster nodes, pods, services, and workloads.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Release Version 3.2.0 (Fase 4) -->
        <div style="position: relative; padding-left: 20px; border-left: 2px solid var(--accent-info);">
          <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px;">
            <h6 style="font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; color: #fff; margin: 0;">v3.2.0</h6>
            <span style="font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-muted);">August 29, 2026</span>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 8px;">
            Smart Storage &amp; Disaster Recovery — Instant Volume Snapshots, 1-Click Rollback Points, and Automated Backup Archive Verification.
          </p>
          <ul style="font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-secondary); padding-left: 16px; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px;">
            <li><strong>Instant Volume Snapshots (Fase 4):</strong> Capture point-in-time recovery archives of <code>/var/www</code> or specific directories before performing risky updates or migrations.</li>
            <li><strong>1-Click Snapshot Rollback (Fase 4):</strong> Instantly restore entire application trees from verified snapshot archives.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Release Version 3.1.0 (Fase 3) -->
        <div style="position: relative; padding-left: 20px; border-left: 2px solid var(--accent-warning);">
          <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px;">
            <h6 style="font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; color: #fff; margin: 0;">v3.1.0</h6>
            <span style="font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-muted);">August 29, 2026</span>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 8px;">
            Autonomous AI Copilot &amp; Smart Operations — Terminal AI Copilot with Natural Language to Shell translation, Safety Guardrails, Predictive Log Anomaly Detection, and Automated RCA Incident Generator.
          </p>
          <ul style="font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-secondary); padding-left: 16px; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px;">
            <li><strong>Terminal AI Copilot (Fase 3):</strong> Translate natural language requests to accurate Linux commands directly in Web Terminal with Safety Guardrails protecting against destructive commands.</li>
            <li><strong>Predictive Log Anomaly Detection (Fase 3):</strong> Proactive background scanner detecting OOM killer warnings, HTTP 502/504 gateway failures, database pool exhaustion, and SSH brute-force bursts.</li>
            <li><strong>Incident Post-Mortem &amp; RCA Generator (Fase 3):</strong> Automated structured Root Cause Analysis report generation with impact timelines and remediation history.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Release Version 3.0.0 -->
        <div style="position: relative; padding-left: 20px; border-left: 2px solid var(--accent-primary);">
          <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px;">
            <h6 style="font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; color: #fff; margin: 0;">v3.0.0</h6>
            <span style="font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-muted);">August 29, 2026</span>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 8px;">
            Major App Ecosystem &amp; Threat Intelligence Release — 1-Click Docker App Store Marketplace (20+ Templates), Container Live Resource Limits &amp; Stats, and Real-Time GeoIP Threat Map with Country Shield.
          </p>
          <ul style="font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-secondary); padding-left: 16px; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px;">
            <li><strong>1-Click Docker App Store (Fase 2):</strong> 20+ curated production-ready application templates across AI &amp; LLM (Ollama, Open WebUI, n8n), Web &amp; CMS (WordPress + MariaDB, Nextcloud, Ghost, Strapi), Dev &amp; Tools (Portainer CE, Uptime Kuma, Vaultwarden, Gitea), Databases (phpMyAdmin, pgAdmin 4, Redis Commander), and Media/IoT (Jellyfin, Home Assistant, Mosquitto MQTT). Includes interactive dynamic form wizard for instant Docker Compose deployment.</li>
            <li><strong>Container Live Resource Limits &amp; Stats (Fase 2):</strong> Real-time monitoring of CPU usage %, Memory usage / limit MB, and Network RX/TX with in-place adjustment of Memory Limits, CPU Quota (NanoCPUs), and Restart Policies directly via Dockerode without restarting or destroying containers.</li>
            <li><strong>Real-Time GeoIP Threat Map &amp; Geo-Shield (Fase 2):</strong> Global attack origin mapping resolving Fail2Ban &amp; WAF intrusion logs into geographic coordinates, top attacking countries breakdown, live blocked attack feed, and 1-Click Geo-Shield country blocking.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Release Version 2.9.0 -->
        <div style="position: relative; padding-left: 20px; border-left: 2px solid var(--accent-info);">
          <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px;">
            <h6 style="font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; color: #fff; margin: 0;">v2.9.0</h6>
            <span style="font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-muted);">August 28, 2026</span>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 8px;">
            Enterprise Security &amp; Mobile PWA Release — Hardware WebAuthn / Passkeys (FIDO2), Progressive Web App (PWA) with WebPush Alerts, and Automated Security Health &amp; CVE Vulnerability Scanner.
          </p>
          <ul style="font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-secondary); padding-left: 16px; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px;">
            <li><strong>WebAuthn / Passkeys (FIDO2) (Fase 1):</strong> True passwordless and biometric authentication (Touch ID, Windows Hello, Face ID, YubiKey) powered by <code>@simplewebauthn/server</code> v13 with multi-device credential management in user settings.</li>
            <li><strong>Progressive Web App &amp; WebPush Notifications (Fase 1):</strong> Native-like mobile and desktop PWA support with Service Worker offline caching and background push notifications for critical server alerts.</li>
            <li><strong>Automated Security Health &amp; Vulnerability Scanner (Fase 1):</strong> Host audit engine scoring system health (0-100), inspecting UFW firewall, SSH hardening, unpatched CVE packages, exposed database ports, and default passwords with 1-click auto-remediation.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Release Version 2.0.0 -->
        <div style="position: relative; padding-left: 20px; border-left: 2px solid var(--accent-success);">
          <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px;">
            <h6 style="font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; color: #fff; margin: 0;">v2.0.0</h6>
            <span style="font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-muted);">July 28, 2026</span>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 8px;">
            Major Architecture &amp; Security Release — Password Policy Engine, Split-View File Manager with CodeMirror &amp; Media Previews, CSP Security Hardening, and 0-Vulnerability Dependency Audit.
          </p>
          <ul style="font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-secondary); padding-left: 16px; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px;">
            <li><strong>Password Policy Engine:</strong> Enforce password complexity rules (length, uppercase, lowercase, numbers, symbols), automated expiration reminder background job, forced change on login (<code>mustChangePassword</code>), audit trail &amp; JSON import/export.</li>
            <li><strong>Split-View File Manager:</strong> Dual-pane interface with side-by-side file tree &amp; editor, smooth draggable divider handle, and full-width responsive flex container.</li>
            <li><strong>Self-Hosted CodeMirror:</strong> Integrated CodeMirror editor with syntax modes, bracket matching, active line highlighting, line numbers, and instant light/dark theme switcher.</li>
            <li><strong>Media &amp; Document Previewer:</strong> Inline previewer for images (with zoom controls &amp; wheel zoom), audio, video, and PDF reader iframe inside split view.</li>
            <li><strong>Tree-to-Editor Drag &amp; Drop:</strong> Drag items from file tree to editor to automatically insert path strings at cursor.</li>
            <li><strong>CSP Nonce Security Hardening:</strong> Automated Content Security Policy nonce injection for all inline scripts &amp; style blocks.</li>
            <li><strong>Rate Limiting &amp; 0 Vulnerabilities:</strong> Refined API &amp; Download Token rate limiters, plus 100% resolution of high-severity npm audit vulnerabilities.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Release Version 1.9.0 -->
        <div style="position: relative; padding-left: 20px; border-left: 2px solid var(--accent-success);">
          <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px;">
            <h6 style="font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; color: #fff; margin: 0;">v1.9.0</h6>
            <span style="font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-muted);">July 17, 2026</span>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 8px;">
            Major feature expansion — 12 new modules including GPU Manager, Power Manager, Mail Server Manager, CDN &amp; Cache Manager, IoT &amp; Edge Device Manager, Enhanced Database Explorer, Runtime Managers, and more.
          </p>
          <ul style="font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-secondary); padding-left: 16px; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px;">
            <li><strong>GPU Manager:</strong> NVIDIA GPU monitoring via nvidia-smi — per-GPU utilization, temperature, fan speed, clocks, CUDA/CUDNN detection, process management with kill, power limit control, GPU reset.</li>
            <li><strong>Power Manager:</strong> CPU governor control &amp; frequency scaling, power profiles (Performance/Balanced/Power-Saver), system sleep (suspend/hibernate/hybrid-sleep), thermal zone monitoring &gt;85&deg;C alerts, fan RPM monitoring.</li>
            <li><strong>Mail Server Manager:</strong> Postfix/Dovecot/SpamAssassin — install/uninstall, domains, email accounts (SHA512-CRYPT), mail queue view/flush/delete-by-ID, SpamAssassin score config, SSL cert viewer, journalctl logs.</li>
            <li><strong>CDN &amp; Cache Manager:</strong> Cloudflare API (zone list, purge all/URL, 24h analytics), Varnish (status/control, VCL editor with syntax validation, cache purge), Redis cache stats (hit/miss/expired) &amp; flush, Full Page Cache (Nginx FPC).</li>
            <li><strong>IoT &amp; Edge Device Manager:</strong> Mosquitto MQTT broker (install/config/users/ACL/publish QoS 0/1/2), Home Assistant &amp; Node-RED Docker deploy, network device discovery via nmap/arp, MQTT metrics.</li>
            <li><strong>Enhanced Database Explorer:</strong> Complete rewrite with 5 tabs — Browse (paginated, sortable), Structure (columns/keys/FK/indexes), Query (SQL console, Ctrl+Enter), Export (JSON/CSV/SQL), Import (CSV/SQL), History (last 100).</li>
            <li><strong>Runtime Managers:</strong> Node.js version management via nvm/nodenv, Python virtual environments via pyenv with Gunicorn/Uvicorn, MongoDB full management panel, Redis keyspace/memory/config manager, Apache virtual host manager.</li>
            <li><strong>Backup &amp; Disaster Recovery:</strong> Rclone + S3 integration — automated scheduled backups, retention policies, one-click restore, offsite backup verification.</li>
            <li><strong>Analytics Dashboard:</strong> Historical metrics with time-range selectors, log aggregation with search/filter, trend analysis charts, exportable reports.</li>
            <li><strong>Multi-User RBAC + SSO/LDAP:</strong> LDAP authentication, SAML/OpenID Connect SSO, fine-grained resource permissions, group-based role mapping.</li>
            <li><strong>Service Mesh &amp; Auto-Healing:</strong> systemd health checks, auto-restart on failure, configurable intervals, alerting, service dependency management.</li>
            <li><strong>Auto-Updater &amp; Rollback:</strong> One-click panel update via git, pre-update health check, automatic rollback on failure, version comparison, update history log.</li>
            <li><strong>Caddy Server Manager:</strong> Full Caddyfile editor with syntax highlighting, automatic HTTPS via Let's Encrypt, reverse proxy config, static file serving, import management.</li>
            <li><strong>AI Auto-Repair &amp; Intelligent Assistant:</strong> GPT-powered log analysis, automatic error pattern detection, intelligent fix suggestions with one-click apply, predictive alerting, self-healing recommendation engine.</li>
            <li><strong>Comprehensive Swagger API Docs:</strong> OpenAPI 3.0 documentation for all 23+ modules with interactive Try-It-Out, search, and categorized browsing.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

